var GR=[["Beast Whistle",20,0,"Adventuring Gear","A bone whistle carved like a gargath that makes a high pitched sound only certain creatures hear well. When you blow it, any beast within 100 ft that hears it knows its distance and direction from you. A friendly beast can be trained to follow signals made with it. After at least 24 hours of training, you can send coded orders to a trained beast within range."],["Breath of the Wind-Touched Jerbeen Figurine",5,0,"Figurine","A cheap figurine, barely more than broken scraps of wood fitted into a rough humanoid shape. Legend says the wood came from branches the Wind-Touched brushed as she flew through the forest."],["Gift of the Wind-Touched Jerbeen Figurine",10,0,"Figurine","A figurine carved from a single piece of wood. It looks hastily made but faintly resembles a jerbeen. Legend says the wood came from the Greenkeeper farmstead."],["Grace of the Wind-Touched Jerbeen Figurine",50,0,"Figurine","A fancy figurine of a winged jerbeen, carved with great skill. Legend says it is made from branches the Wind-Touched gave from her own forest home."],["Designer Clothes",30,6,"Clothing","Zephyr & Co. sells outfits by famed tailors across the Wood. Each costs 30 gp, twice the price of ordinary fine clothes, and lets the wearer look like a high society perch dweller. Choose a brand from the Designer Fashions table or roll to see what the shop has in stock."],["Dustbloom Spices",5,1,"Trade Good","Spices from the faraway Dustbloom desert, prized for their unusual peppery flavor."],["Elderberry Everwine",25,2,"Trade Good","A fine everwine made from elderberries that forest vintners grow with special care. The Alderheart elite prize it for its rich aroma and dry sweetness."],["Firelance Venom",300,0,"Poison","Venom taken from the sac of a dead or incapacitated firelance. A creature exposed to it makes a DC 11 Constitution save, taking 14 (4d6) poison damage on a fail or half on a success. If this poison damage drops a creature to 0 hit points, it is Poisoned for 1 hour even after regaining hit points. A single dose costs 300 gp."],["Gargath Wool Clothes",10,8,"Clothing","Warm, heavy clothing from the Gargan Steppe, made of spun gargath wool lined with coarse fur. The wearer stays comfortable in temperatures as low as -50 degrees Fahrenheit."],["Gasparian Tree Nuts",2,1,"Trade Good","Large hollow nuts from the Gasparian Isles. The sweet white flesh can be eaten and the hollow holds a tasty liquid. They are popular in sweets."],["Imported Fruits",3,1,"Trade Good","Fresh fruits from lands beyond the Songsea, in high demand among the nobility of Alderheart."],["Noble's Jewelry",150,1,"Clothing","A set of designer jewelry fit for a high society socialite. Worn with fine clothes, it lets you pass as a noble. Custom made pieces cost 10 gp extra."],["Perfume",20,0,"Adventuring Gear","A scented liquid made from rare floral extracts, wakewyrm ambergris, and essential oils. Dabbed on skin, fur, or feathers, it leaves you smelling pleasant for 8 hours. A small stoppered crystal vial holds 20 uses."],["Sage's Trinket",0,0,"Adventuring Gear","A small keepsake rolled on a d10. 1 a teacup painted with an indigo talon emblem. 2 a raptor's claw. 3 a handwritten ticket for one free hug on wrinkled parchment. 4 a tiny cheese wheel in red wax. 5 a miniature bronze emberbat figurine. 6 a porcelain thimble shaped like a gallus beak. 7 a dark velvet sachet of dried lavender. 8 a tuft of strig feathers tied with a worn bowstring. 9 a green silk handkerchief embroidered with red strawberries. 10 a small burlap pouch marked seebies, full of corn kernels."],["Steppe Rations",25,0.5,"Trade Good","Small bars of smoked plants, dried berries, ground nuts, and honey baked into a chewy block. A bar does not fill you for a full day of travel, but holds off hunger for 2 hours. The spices warm you from within. Eating a bar gives Resistance to cold damage for 1 hour. You can gain this benefit for only 1 hour per day."],["Tea",5,1,"Trade Good","High quality tea leaves, dried and ready to brew."],["Traveler's Guide",25,2,"Adventuring Gear","A handy book with detailed information on one big city or notable destination chosen by the GM. Most were written by Jonall, though other well known explorers wrote some. It lets you add your Proficiency Bonus to Intelligence checks about the destination it covers."],["Traveler's Lantern",12,1,"Adventuring Gear","A compact hooded lantern with a large metal ring on top, so you can hang it from a belt or sash and still get light. It sheds bright light in a 15 ft radius and dim light for another 15 ft. Once lit it burns 6 hours on a flask (1 pint) of oil. As an action, lower the hood to cut the light to dim light in a 5 ft radius."]];
